\details{
The user inputs for this module are separated from the outputs to allow for
more flexible UI design.

The module draws the heatmap of the top differentially expressed genes of a
bulk experiment: genes passing adjusted p-value and fold-change cut-offs are
ranked, the top ones taken from the transformed counts, and shown as per-gene
z-scores across the samples, split into up- and down-regulated blocks with the
sample metadata as annotations.

\code{data} is a list holding the experiment and its results,
\verb{list(object = <SummarizedExperiment>, results = <data frame>)}, where the
results are a DESeq2 \code{results()} table (a \code{DataFrame} will do), an edgeR
\code{topTags()} table, a limma \code{topTable()} or any table with an adjusted p-value
and a log2 fold change per gene; or a \code{SummarizedExperiment} whose \code{rowData}
carries those columns. Results are matched to the experiment's genes through
its row names, by the results' row names or an identifier column.

The heatmap is drawn by \code{\link[VizModules:ComplexHeatmap_HeatmapInputsUI]{VizModules::ComplexHeatmap_HeatmapInputsUI()}}, so
its scaling, clustering, colour, label and annotation controls all apply;
those inputs are documented there. The rows carry \code{direction} ("Up"/"Down")
and \code{log2FC} as row annotations; every \code{colData} column is available as a
column annotation, keyed by the \code{sample} column.

\strong{This module is not plotly.} It renders through InteractiveComplexHeatmap,
so the shared plotly tabs do not apply, and it needs ComplexHeatmap,
InteractiveComplexHeatmap and circlize.
}
